*Network Threats 

Malware - Malicious Software 

Propagation Mechanism - The techniques malware uses to spread

Payloads - The Malicious actions taken by malware

Virus - malicious software program that infects files or systems, replicating itself by inserting its own code

Worms - Malware spread on its own by exploiting vulnerablilites 

Trojan - A malware that disguises itself as a legitimate, harmless software 

Botnets A network of Hijacked, connected devices secretly controlled by a single entity

Man in The Browser - Attacks exploits flaws in the browsers and browser plugins

Replay Attack - When someone intercepts and fraudulently records data, then resends it to receiver
(protection) Token, Timestamp

SSl Stripping - Tricks browsers into using unencrypted communications 

Fault Injection attacks - Hardware hacking technique where an attacker temporarily stresses a device to make
it glitch or malfunction 

Side Channel Attacks - Security exploit that breaks system by observing its physical side effects 

*Threat Detection and Prevention

(IDS) Intrusion Detection System - A system that monitors network traffic for signs of malicious activity 

(IPS) Intrusion Prevention System - A system that blocks malicious activity automatically

False Positive Error - System triggers and alerts when attack did not actually happen 

False Negative Error - System fails to trigger an alert when an actual attack occurs

Signature Detection System - A system that scans network traffic for unique digital "fingerprints" of known malware 

Anomaly Detection System - A system that learns what "normal" looks like in your data and flags anything 
outside of that pattern

*Malware Prevention 

Antimalware - Protects system against many different softwate threats 

Signature Detective - Watches for known patterns of malware activity 

Behavior Detection - Watches for deviations from normal patterns of activity 

(EDR) Endpoint Detection and Response - Advanced security system that constantly monitors devices like laptops, desktops
and servers

Sandboxing - An isolated digital safezone

Port Scanners - A tool that checks system to see which communication pathways (ports) are open and accepting data

Vulnerability Scanner - A tool that scans your computers, networks for known security weaknesses before hackers can exploit

(nmap) Network Mapper - A tool used to discover devices and understand the security layout of a network

Nessus - widely used vulnerability scanning tool that detects security weaknesses across networks, 
systems, and applications.















